REFERENCE   1
  CONSRTM   Wellcome Sanger Tree of Life Programme
  TITLE     Direct Submission
  JOURNAL   Submitted (07-MAY-2022) WELLCOME SANGER INSTITUTE, Tree of Life,
            Wellcome Genome Campus, Hinxton CB10 1SA, United Kingdom
COMMENT     The assembly wpSthLimi1.1 is based on 45x PacBio data, 10X Genomics
            Chromium data, and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of
            Life Project (https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly
            process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio
            assembly generation with Hifiasm, retained haplotig separation with
            purge_dups, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial
            genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, the primary assembly
            was analysed and manually improved using gEVAL. Chromosome-scale
            scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of
            size. Scaffold order and orientation is uncertain chromosome 6
            0.39-8.86mb.  Heterozygous inversion chromosome 7 76.84-95.76mb.
